 ## Overview
-The 3D Super-Resolution (SR) Module is a deep learning-based component designed to reconstruct high-resolution volumetric data from low-resolution inputs, often serving as the final refinement stage in implicit neural representation (INR) pipelines [S1]. It addresses reconstruction artifacts, such as ringing and blurring, by reconstructing the original high-resolution volume from the INR output using deep learning, providing intrinsic denoising and reducing reconstruction artefacts [S1]. Unlike standard interpolation, this module employs a 3D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) integrated with an Attention Mechanism to prioritize significant features, thereby restoring resolution to levels close to the original while providing intrinsic denoising [S1].
+The 3D Super-Resolution (SR) Module reconstructs high-resolution volumetric data from low-resolution inputs generated by an Implicit Neural Representation (INR), providing intrinsic denoising and reducing reconstruction artifacts such as ringing and blurring [S1]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Contrastive Diffusion for Volume Super-Resolution (CD-TVD)](10411-contrastive-diffusion-for-volume-super-resolution-cd-tvd.md) by employing a deterministic deep learning pipeline based on the SRNO architecture, which prioritizes significant features via an attention mechanism rather than probabilistic diffusion processes [S1].
 
